,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.426304818,"data":"    DECOMPOSITION of the 20.5 s warm call:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.427057834,"data":"        4.58 s   Python constructing UOps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.427773617,"data":"       15.82 s   TinyGrad's SCHEDULER (rewrite passes)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.428575884,"data":"        0.11 s   GPU execution (measured separately in perf_kda.py)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.429334156,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.430079111,"data":"    So it is NOT '99% Python'. It is mostly SCHEDULER.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.430774003,"data":"    The kernels ARE compiled once -- COLD is 49.5 s and WARM does not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.431523365,"data":"    recompile -- but tinygrad re-runs every rewrite pass on every\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.432218547,"data":"    realize(), because there is no separation between 'compile' and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.432891702,"data":"    'execute' in the API. A replay path that cached the SCHEDULED\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.433641192,"data":"    PROGRAM LIST, not just the compiled kernels, would bring the per-call\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1928.434415397,"data":"    cost down to the 109 ms of GPU time.\n"}
